@startuml fig3-register
!include style.iuml
title Figure 3 (revises 2.2 Figure 3): Register an account (FR 1.1, FR 1.2, NFR 4; A3, R1)

actor User
participant ":RegisterActivity" as UI
participant ":AuthViewModel" as VM
participant ":InputValidator" as V
participant ":AuthRepository" as R
participant "auth :\nFirebaseAuth" as A
participant "db :\nFirebaseFirestore" as DB

User -> UI : enter name, USC email, USC ID,\npassword, <b>confirm password</b>; tap Create account
UI -> VM : register(name, email, uscId, password, <b>confirm</b>)
VM -> V : validateRegistration(name, email, uscId,\npassword, <b>confirm</b>)
V --> VM : result
alt result is not valid
  VM --> UI : <b>fieldError (LiveData)</b>
  UI --> User : error shown <b>on that field</b>, no account created
else result is valid
  VM -> R : register(name, <b>normalized email</b>, uscId, password,\n<b>nowMillis</b>, cb)
  R -> A : <b>createUserWithEmailAndPassword(email, password)</b>
  note right of R
    CHANGED: the account is created first, so the
    USC ID check below runs as a signed-in user and
    uscIds can stay unreadable to signed-out users (NFR 4)
  end note
  alt email already registered
    A --> R : FirebaseAuthUserCollisionException
    R --> VM : cb.onFailure(<b>"An account with this USC email already exists."</b>)
    VM --> UI : <b>error (Event)</b>
  else account created (password stored as a hash)
    A --> R : firebaseUser
    R -> DB : <b>runTransaction: get uscIds/{uscId};</b>\n<b>if absent set uscIds/{uscId} and users/{uid}</b>
    alt USC ID already reserved, or the write failed
      DB --> R : <b>transaction aborted</b>
      R -> A : <b>firebaseUser.delete(); signOut()</b>
      note right of R
        NEW: roll back the half-created
        login so the email can be reused
      end note
      R --> VM : cb.onFailure(<b>"An account with this USC ID already exists."</b>\n<b>or, if the write itself failed, the FirebaseErrors message</b>)
      VM --> UI : <b>error (Event)</b>
    else both documents written atomically (FR 1.2)
      DB --> R : success
      R --> VM : cb.onSuccess(user)
      VM --> UI : currentUser = user (LiveData)
      UI --> User : open GroupListActivity
    end
  end
end

legend bottom left
<b>Bold</b> messages and notes marked NEW or CHANGED are departures from Project 2.2; plain = unchanged.
endlegend
@enduml
